Moreinfo:
I build teams who can make software running in the Cloud under high load.

- 10 years of experience in IT, 8+ of which as a full-time Business/System Analyst 
- Bachelor in CS, Master's in System Analysis 
- Domains: Telecom, eCommerce, AdTech, Manufacturing, Web, Mobile; familiar with Cloud (AWS)
- Performed roles: Technical Writer, System Analyst, Business Analyst, Technical Product Owner, Scrum Master.
- Coordinated work of backend, web and mobile teams (Android, IOS).
- 5 successfully delivered large scale projects.

Today I help a US-based public company run a team of 8-10 engineers as a Scrum Master.  program with multiple initiatives to decompose a monolithic, up-and-running system into microservices to achieve scalability and enable the company’s global expansion.

What I do:
- collaborate with business & end users to elicit the needs & set expectations;
- collaborate with Product, UI/UX & architecture in terms of a technical solution, limitations & NFRs;
- translate PRD into Jira tasks, write stories and ACs;
- manage Jira backlog;
- drive Scrum ceremonies;
- resolve blockers;
- coordinate cross-team dependencies within the program and their alignment to the release schedule of an organization overall;
- manage releases.

I am seeking an opportunity to transition to Product Management. I will be an excellent addition to your team if you're looking for someone with a technical background.

Looking For:
Expectations:
- Support of changes/transformations from board members/C** level;
- Participation in a company (or startup) engaged in the development of innovative products
- Working on team and organization level;

Highlights:
Recent projects:
"Legal management system" (full cycle multi-attorney workflow from filing a claim to executive proceedings); 

CRM system for one of the largest wholesale suppliers of tourism products (hundreds of customers, tens of thousands of products, several warehouses in different cities); 

SaaS management platform for fitness, dance clubs and same type small businesses; several online stores of varying complexity.

candidate_profile:
Position:
Automation QA Engineer

Moreinfo:
#1
Project: Premium virtual reality + streaming/video platform
Position: General QA Engineer
Term: 04/2021 - 09/2022
Responsibilities: 
- Performing regression and functional testing in JavaScript
(using WebDriverIO, Puppeteer frameworks + Axios for API
requests);
- Testing the API using special tools like Insomnia/Postman, and Swagger;
- Writing and maintaining test documentation;
- Conducting functional, regression, and smoke testing;
- Detecting, reporting, and tracking defects in Jira;
- Working and communicating with developers, project
managers and others to set and meet the quality standards
and deadlines;
- Using GitHub to maintain and manage the build scripts and
other documentation related to the project;
- Working on the project using Agile + Kanban methodologies.

#2
Project: Healthcare domain
Position: Automation QA Engineer
Term: 11/2022 - 05/2023
Responsibilities:
-Working and maintaining automation testing framework (based on WebDriverIO) + implementing new features & methods;
-Using Git + BitBucket as a main VCS + CI/CD platform;
-Testing the API using Postman & Swagger;
-Using JIRA as a main bug-tracking + task-management platform;
-Using Scrum methodology to build & organize the main working processes.


#3
Project: Mobile App - Food order/delivery
Position: Automation QA Engineer
Term: 09/2022 - Present
Responsibilities:
-Building automation mobile testing framework from scratch, using WDIO + Appium as a basis;
-Setup API auto-tests from scratch using Playwright + Axios (for custom methods)
-Using JIRA as a main bug-tracking + task-management platform;
-Testing the API using Postman & Swagger;
-Using Git + GitLab as a main VCS;
-Using Scrum methodology to build & organize the main working processes;

English Level:
upper

Experience Years:
2.5

